From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Attard <sattard@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:52:51 +0000
Subject: feat: key code caches to the patch set and the embedded blob

V8 keys serialized code (JS code caches and serialized wasm modules) on
Version::Hash(), i.e. on major.minor.build.patch only. Electron applies
V8 fixes on release branches as patches without changing that version
number, so a build with a different patch set still accepts serialized
code written by the previous release. Serialized wasm code stores calls
to builtins as raw Builtin ids, so when a patch adds, removes or reorders
a builtin the deserialized code is relinked against the wrong builtins
and crashes or traps at runtime.

This adds two things:

* a v8_version_hash_salt GN arg that is mixed into Version::Hash(), plus
  v8_version_hash_salt_files to derive the salt at gn gen time from a
  list of files. Electron points the latter at patches/v8 (see
  build/args/all.gn), so any change to the patch set invalidates every
  code cache and every serialized wasm module. The salt reaches
  version.cc through a header written at gn gen time so that changing it
  recompiles one file.
* the embedded blob's data and code hashes in the serialized wasm module
  header, so that a module is only ever deserialized into a build whose
  builtins are identical to the one that produced it, whatever the
  version number says.

Both parts are suitable for upstreaming.

